# Study guide / blog standards

When creating or editing pages under `app/study-guides/`:

## Always use shared components
- `StudyGuideShell` for page chrome (header, article card, FAQ, footer)
- `StudyGuideLangTabs` for English + Marathi bilingual posts
- `StudyGuideTable` for tables (never raw unstyled `<table>` in new blogs)
- `StudyGuideCallout` for key tip boxes
- `STUDY_GUIDE_PROSE_CLASS` from `lib/studyGuideStyles.ts` if writing single-language prose

## Readability / spacing
- Never wrap the article body in `not-prose` — that kills Tailwind list/bullet styles for all descendants. Put `not-prose` only on chrome (tabs, ads, custom widgets).
- Use `study-guide-prose` + `STUDY_GUIDE_PROSE_CLASS` for normal readable bullets/numbers with light spacing (not card-style lists)
- For topic breakdowns (e.g. Land Revenue points), prefer `h4` header + short paragraph instead of stuffing title and detail into one bullet
- Prefer short paragraphs (2–4 sentences)
- Use full sentences in lists and FAQs — no telegram fragments
- Section headings (`h3`) should breathe: leave normal paragraph space before/after
- FAQ cards use `space-y-4`; do not pack FAQ items tightly

## Language quality
- Polish English grammar before shipping (no slang fragments like “bubble the OMR”)
- Marathi should read naturally for Maharashtra aspirants — not word-for-word machine translation
- FAQ answers should be complete in both languages when the page is bilingual
- Prefer “practise for free” / clear exam English over hype copy

## Content structure for new blogs
1. Strong opening (1–3 paragraphs)
2. One callout with the key takeaway
3. Numbered sections with scannable lists/tables
4. Free practice links back to `/exams`, mocks, related guides
5. FAQ + schema when useful for SEO

## Ads
Use:
```tsx
<DisplayAd adsenseSlot={IN_CONTENT_AD_SLOT} ezoicKey="contentInline" className="my-8 not-prose" />
```
Never invent a `slot=` prop.

## Wire-up
- Add card to `app/study-guides/page.tsx`
- Append path to `ADDITIONAL_DISCOVERY_ENTRIES` in `app/sitemap.ts`
